<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-asteroxylon-mackiei-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Asteroxylon mackiei Schnakenberg critical wavelength at 5.2 µm (Pass 1) — MorphoEval overall 84.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1 implements Schnakenberg kinetics with the critical wavelength fixed at 5.2 µm (k_c = 2π/5.2e-6 m⁻¹), δ = D_v/D_u = 160, and a periodic 156 µm × 117 µm tracheid-file window (30 critical wavelengths). The homogeneous state has trace -0.16 and determinant 1. σ(k_c) = 0.396 and the equal-diffusion control has σ_max = -0.080. A δ sweep at fixed D_u shortens the wavelength monotonically. The basic look composites the activator onto a CC BY-SA compression fossil (Kenraiz); full-frame grayscale Pearson r = 0.98950 and RMSE = 7.425 gray levels. The plate's spectral centroid of the activator is 7.646 µm, not 5.2 µm. Age is 407 Ma. Not yet scored at Pass 1: a row hold-out, a gray-level KS, and a measured axis-envelope wavelength. The measurement sidecar is regenerated from the final module, so it also lists those three Pass 2 numbers; this audit's morphometric score does not credit them. Overall 84.5/100 (faithfulness 83.6, reproducibility 86.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8f0e4833ae7c01aa84482096856ead2148c3f912; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 80, Parameter expressivity 86, Morphometric validation 82, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/asteroxylon_mackiei_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-asteroxylon-mackiei-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 8f0e4833ae7c01aa84482096856ead2148c3f912, image/png, 816591 B, 1344×960 px, artifact_sha256 fd44e2c72e7684d805d6919d20e45779d6d498602ffa1c6da45d662ccf945eee (sha256 fd44e2c72e7684d805d6919d20e45779d6d498602ffa1c6da45d662ccf945eee), spec_fingerprint 716e903fe3a6b195756b816d8895f02c8c7f83e58d092ed921cdf0ea6a927c85. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 716e903fe3a6b195756b816d8895f02c8c7f83e58d092ed921cdf0ea6a927c85; artifact_sha256: fd44e2c72e7684d805d6919d20e45779d6d498602ffa1c6da45d662ccf945eee; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/asteroxylon_mackiei_turing_wavelength_s0/README.md=8d4cec453c791d09..., datasets/asteroxylon_mackiei_turing_wavelength_s0/asteroxylon_mackiei_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=9577842bd82c5dae..., datasets/asteroxylon_mackiei_turing_wavelength_s0/asteroxylon_mackiei_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=ad3ca375be91c9cf..., datasets/asteroxylon_mackiei_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=345af56bd8c1eb6a..., datasets/asteroxylon_mackiei_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=95e0c02c8d34e83a...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Kidston & Lang 1920: Asteroxylon mackiei has an actinostele and leaf traces into microphylls (DOI 10.1017/s0080456800004506). | Edwards, Kenrick & Dolan 2017: the Rhynie Chert is an Early Devonian (Pragian) terrestrial deposit, taken here as 407 Ma. | Turing 1952: a finite critical wavenumber k_c when inhibitor and activator diffuse at different rates. | Schnakenberg 1979: the two-species kinetics used for the calibration. | Hetherington et al. 2021: evidence-based whole-plant habit of Asteroxylon mackiei.; reconstructed_in_script: D_u is solved so that λ_c = 5.2 µm at δ = 160; the domain is 30 wavelengths long (156 µm). | Fourier pseudospectral integration of the periodic Schnakenberg system, seed 3124. | δ sweep at fixed D_u and an equal-diffusion ablation (σ_max < 0). | Basic-look composite of the activator onto the Kenraiz plate at fixed α = 0.32.; transfer_boundary: The vendored photograph is a centimetre-scale compression. Metres per pixel are the model scale bar, not a thin-section calibration. | 5.2 µm is this slot's detail-tier wavelength. It is not a published histological period for Asteroxylon pigment.; does_not_claim: Does not claim the PDE reconstructs microphyll phyllotaxis from a homogeneous shoot. | Does not claim the 283 µm enation-sibling parameters; that wavelength is only the scale ratio 54.5. | Does not claim Cooksonia or a Baragwanathia-grade successor was simulated. | Does not claim a signed nanopublication; no local nanopub profile was present.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Choose activator contrast on the top 75% of rows only and report Pearson r on the held-out bottom 25%.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Add a two-sample KS distance between the plate and the last-frame gray histograms, with reference 0.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Measure the leafy-axis envelope wavelength in micrometres under the model scale bar and set it beside 5.2 µm.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.45e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

