<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-asteroxylon-mackiei-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Asteroxylon mackiei Schnakenberg critical wavelength at 5.2 µm (Pass 1) (Asteroxylon mackiei (Early Devonian Rhynie Chert lycopsid))",
        "Asteroxylon mackiei Schnakenberg critical wavelength at 5.2 µm (Pass 1) faithfully reproduces Asteroxylon mackiei (Early Devonian Rhynie Chert lycopsid) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-asteroxylon-mackiei-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-asteroxylon-mackiei-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-asteroxylon-mackiei-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-asteroxylon-mackiei-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-asteroxylon-mackiei-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Asteroxylon mackiei (Early Devonian Rhynie Chert lycopsid) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-asteroxylon-mackiei-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Asteroxylon mackiei (Early Devonian Rhynie Chert lycopsid)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim Cooksonia or a Baragwanathia-grade successor was simulated.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim a signed nanopublication; no local nanopub profile was present.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the 283 µm enation-sibling parameters; that wavelength is only the scale ratio 54.5.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the PDE reconstructs microphyll phyllotaxis from a homogeneous shoot.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Basic-look composite of the activator onto the Kenraiz plate at fixed α = 0.32.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: D_u is solved so that λ_c = 5.2 µm at δ = 160; the domain is 30 wavelengths long (156 µm).",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Fourier pseudospectral integration of the periodic Schnakenberg system, seed 3124.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: δ sweep at fixed D_u and an equal-diffusion ablation (σ_max < 0).",
        "reported_in_source: Edwards, Kenrick & Dolan 2017: the Rhynie Chert is an Early Devonian (Pragian) terrestrial deposit, taken here as 407 Ma.",
        "reported_in_source: Hetherington et al. 2021: evidence-based whole-plant habit of Asteroxylon mackiei.",
        "reported_in_source: Kidston & Lang 1920: Asteroxylon mackiei has an actinostele and leaf traces into microphylls (DOI 10.1017/s0080456800004506).",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979: the two-species kinetics used for the calibration.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952: a finite critical wavenumber k_c when inhibitor and activator diffuse at different rates.",
        "transfer_boundary: 5.2 µm is this slot's detail-tier wavelength. It is not a published histological period for Asteroxylon pigment.",
        "transfer_boundary: The vendored photograph is a centimetre-scale compression. Metres per pixel are the model scale bar, not a thin-section calibration." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Asteroxylon mackiei (Early Devonian (Pragian Rhynie Chert, 407 Ma))" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "III. Phyta (Embryophyta)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Angiospermae & Gymnospermae" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Asteroxylon" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-asteroxylon-mackiei-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/asteroxylon_mackiei_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Asteroxylon mackiei (Early Devonian Rhynie Chert lycopsid); environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Kidston & Lang 1920: Asteroxylon mackiei has an actinostele and leaf traces into microphylls (DOI 10.1017/s0080456800004506). | Edwards, Kenrick & Dolan 2017: the Rhynie Chert is an Early Devonian (Pragian) terrestrial deposit, taken here as 407 Ma. | Turing 1952: a finite critical wavenumber k_c when inhibitor and activator diffuse at different rates. | Schnakenberg 1979: the two-species kinetics used for the calibration. | Hetherington et al. 2021: evidence-based whole-plant habit of Asteroxylon mackiei.; reconstructed_in_script: D_u is solved so that λ_c = 5.2 µm at δ = 160; the domain is 30 wavelengths long (156 µm). | Fourier pseudospectral integration of the periodic Schnakenberg system, seed 3124. | δ sweep at fixed D_u and an equal-diffusion ablation (σ_max < 0). | Basic-look composite of the activator onto the Kenraiz plate at fixed α = 0.32.; transfer_boundary: The vendored photograph is a centimetre-scale compression. Metres per pixel are the model scale bar, not a thin-section calibration. | 5.2 µm is this slot's detail-tier wavelength. It is not a published histological period for Asteroxylon pigment.; does_not_claim: Does not claim the PDE reconstructs microphyll phyllotaxis from a homogeneous shoot. | Does not claim the 283 µm enation-sibling parameters; that wavelength is only the scale ratio 54.5. | Does not claim Cooksonia or a Baragwanathia-grade successor was simulated. | Does not claim a signed nanopublication; no local nanopub profile was present.]; phenomenon_size: 5.7 µm (5.668e-06 m, log10=-5.247 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 5.7 µm to 1.3 cm): 5.7 µm:asteroxylon-mackiei-bioelectric-polarity, 18 µm:asteroxylon-mackiei-vertex-packing, 283 µm:asteroxylon-mackiei-turing-wavelength, 567 µm:asteroxylon-mackiei-clock-wavefront, 1.3 mm:asteroxylon-mackiei-morphogen-condensation, 1.6 mm:asteroxylon-mackiei-elastic-buckling, 1.8 mm:asteroxylon-mackiei-flux-canalization, 2.5 mm:asteroxylon-mackiei-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1017/s0080456800004506>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.1952.0012>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rstb.2016.0489>,
        <https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.69447> ;
    pk:externalAtlasDataset <https://paleobiodb.org/classic/checkTaxonInfo?taxon_name=Asteroxylon>,
